== Noodles ==

Cut the @rice noodle sheets{4%oz}(fresh) into strips 1 1/2 inches wide and put them in a bowl.

> With dried @?wide rice noodles{2%oz} instead: soak in 1 quart boiling water ~{15-20%minutes} until pliable, drain, rinse three times in cold water, and toss with @?neutral oil{1%tsp}.

== Sauce ==

Whisk together @Thai oyster sauce{2%tbsp}, @fish sauce{1%tbsp}, @Thai thin soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @granulated sugar{1/2%tsp} and @ground white pepper{1/4%tsp}.

== Stir-fry ==

Pound the @garlic{4%cloves}(peeled) and @Thai chiles{7}(red, fresh, stemmed) to a rough paste in a #mortar and pestle{}.

Heat a #wok{} over high heat until it just smokes. Add @neutral oil{2%tbsp}, then the garlic paste, and stir ~{30%seconds} until fragrant but not brown. Lower the heat if the garlic starts to colour.

Back on high, add the @fingerroot{1/2%oz}(julienned), @makrut lime leaves{5}(fresh, ribs removed) and @pork shoulder{3%oz}(sliced very thin, about 1 by 1 1/2 inches). Stir ~{40%seconds} until the pork is nearly cooked.

Add the @long beans{1%oz}(cut on the bias into 1-inch pieces), @baby corn{1%oz}(cut into 1/2-inch pieces) and @Chinese broccoli{1 1/2%oz}(cut on the bias into 1 1/2-inch pieces). Stir hard until they begin to char in spots.

Add the noodles and pour the sauce around the edge of the wok. Toss ~{2%minutes} until the noodles have soaked it all up.

Off the heat, stir in the @red long chile{2}(seeded, sliced 1/4 inch on the bias) and @holy basil leaves{1/4%cup} until the basil wilts.

Serve at once with more @fish sauce{}, @ground white pepper{}, @Thai chile flakes{}, @granulated sugar{} and @chili vinegar{} on the table.
